      "guidance": "Generated component owns the timer handle, the time base, one compare unit in PWM mode 1 with preload, the channel and the pad. Use the returned interface; do not initialize the timer, the channel or the pad again. Supports only the listed frequencies at the captured 144MHz kernel clock: each has an exact prescaler and period, the period is at least 1000 counts and full duty fits a 16-bit compare register. Duty is thousandths of the period rounded down to a whole count; the duty in force from a period boundary on is the last one written before it. The first period after a start can be shorter at the pad, never longer. start and stop belong to one thread; set duty may also run in an interrupt. Active high, counting up, internal clock; no dithering, complementary output, dead time, break input, one-pulse or any other channel of the timer. On a timer with a break function the SDK sets the main output enable when the channel starts. The level of the pad while stopped is not established. Init verifies the clock and register factors; dynamic clock changes are outside the contract. Build is not a measurement of frequency, duty or edge quality.",
