          "setup": "Already initialized after mx_system_init. Header bkpt_components/{{unit}}.h; private timer handle, time base, compare unit, channel and pad. No manual timer, channel or GPIO setup.",
          "start": "{{unit}}_start(duty_permille), 0..1000: checked HAL_OK restarts the counter and then enables the nominal {{frequency_hz}}Hz output, so the first period at the pad can be shorter than a full one and every later period is whole. One thread only, never from an interrupt; fails while running.",
          "set_duty": "{{unit}}_set_duty(duty_permille), 0..1000, rounded down to a whole count of the {{period}}+1 count period: checked HAL_OK; the duty in force from a period boundary on is the last one written before it. Fails unless running. Owning thread or an interrupt; an interrupt that preempts start or stop gets a failure until start has finished and from the moment stop begins.",
